            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A handheld fluid delivery device is provided. The device comprises a housing having at least a portion sized and shaped to be handheld by a user. The housing comprises an electrically conductive portion configured to be grasped by said user during operation and electrically connected to a direct current battery. The device further comprises a reservoir configured to contain a fluid and at least one nozzle in fluid communication with said reservoir. The direct current battery is configured to power delivery of the fluid from the reservoir to the at least one nozzle. The device also has an electrode assembly configured to electrostatically charge the fluid. A plurality of electrodes of the electrode assembly is configured to emit ions parallel to a flow pathway of the fluid emitted from the at least one nozzle such that the plurality of electrodes form a static electrical field through which the fluid passes.</p>
            </abstract>
